# chip_tracks, with the H ORIGINS PLACED FOR A MIRRORED LAYOUT.
#
# The PATTERNS here are byte-identical to chip_tracks.buda — same stack, same
# widths, same 10 signals per period, same periods, same overheads, same 504
# grid.  THE ONLY DIFFERENCE IS THREE H ORIGINS: M4 -199, M6 -403.5, M8 -802
# (against -200 / -400 / -800).  Everything else in this file is a copy.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE.  A flipped instance's routing is its reference's routing
# reflected about the instance's own centreline, so the layer's pattern must be
# invariant under that reflection — the centreline must land on a reflection
# AXIS of the pattern.  Two things are needed and they are independent:
#
#   1. the pattern must HAVE axes at all -- it must be a palindrome.  That is
#      now true in chip_tracks.buda itself (each rail centred in its gap), so
#      this file inherits it and no longer has to change any slot.
#   2. the ORIGIN must put an axis ON the instance centrelines.  That is what
#      is left, and it is placement-specific, which is why it cannot live in
#      the shared file: chip_stack's three flipped instances sit at centres
#      8694 / 10710 / 12222, all differing by multiples of 504, so one origin
#      per layer serves all three -- but they are THIS design's centres.
#
# The condition is  instance_centre - origin == axis  (mod period/2), and each
# layer's axis sits at the power-rail centre (rail/2), so:
#
#   layer  period  axis (mod p/2)  origin  shift
#   M2       18     1  (mod 9)     -100    none needed
#   M4       18     1  (mod 9)     -199    +1
#   M6       24     1.5 (mod 12)   -403.5  -3.5
#   M8       56     4  (mod 28)    -802    -2
#
# M10 CANNOT be satisfied and does not need to be: its half period 37 does not
# divide 504, so the three flipped centres fall on three different residues and
# no single origin serves them.  That is precisely why `reserve_top_layers 2`
# caps cells at M9 — the grid is the LCM over the layers the CELLS use, and M10
# is not one of them.
#
# The V origins are the shared file's: an upside-down flip maps y -> 2d-y and
# leaves x alone, so vertical tracks take no part in this.
def_layer  2 M2  H LOW 55.56
def_layer  3 M3  V LOW 55.56
def_layer  4 M4  H TOP 55.56
def_layer  5 M5  V TOP 55.56
def_layer  6 M6  H TOP 66.67
def_layer  7 M7  V TOP 58.97
def_layer  8 M8  H TOP 57.14
def_layer  9 M9  V TOP 57.14
def_layer 10 M10 H TOP 56.76
def_layer 11 M11 V TOP 56.76

# H layers — symmetric units (rail centred in its gap), periods unchanged.
def_track_pattern 2  -100   POWER 2 0.625  SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.625  GROUND 2 0.625  SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.625
def_track_pattern 4  -199   POWER 2 0.625  SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.625  GROUND 2 0.625  SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.625
def_track_pattern 6  -403.5 POWER 3 0.75  SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.75  GROUND 3 0.75  SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.5 SIGNAL 0.5 0.75
def_track_pattern 8  -802   POWER 8 1.375  SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 1.375  GROUND 8 1.375  SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 1.375
def_track_pattern 10 -1200  POWER 10 2  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 2  GROUND 10 2  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 2

# V layers — unchanged from chip_tracks.buda (a y-flip does not move them).
def_track_pattern 3  0      POWER 2 0.625  SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.625  GROUND 2 0.625  SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.625
def_track_pattern 5  0      POWER 2 0.625  SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.625  GROUND 2 0.625  SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.25 SIGNAL 0.5 0.625
def_track_pattern 7  -600   POWER 6 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 1  GROUND 6 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 0.5 SIGNAL 1 1
def_track_pattern 9  -1000  POWER 8 1.375  SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 1.375  GROUND 8 1.375  SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 0.75 SIGNAL 1.5 1.375
def_track_pattern 11 -1400  POWER 10 2  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 2  GROUND 10 2  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 2

report_overhead
